--
N5008 [dcl.init.aggr]/4-5: in `B b{{}, {owner(7), 3}}' with `struct B :
E { A a; }' the member a (an aggregate with a non-POD member owner) is
aggregate-initialized from {owner(7), 3}.  The aggregate-with-base path
in cpp_constructor builds an initializer_list value for a, and symex
stops with an invariant violation ("Reached unimplemented
boolbv_widtht::get_entry()").  bin53 fails as well.  g++ 13 (with
-fsanitize=address) and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only
its WRONG assertion.
